  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Switchin' the positions for you \n\nCookin' in the kitchen, and I'm in the bedroom \n\nI'm in the Olympics, way I'm jumpin' through hoops \n\nKnow my love infinite, nothin' I wouldn't do \n\nThat I won't do, switchin' for you\n\nChef has an array AAA consisting of NNN integers.\n\nChef can swap two elements on positions iii and jjj (1≤i&lt;j≤N)(1\\le i\\lt j \\le N)(1≤i&lt;j≤N) only if:\n\n\nAiA_iAi​ &amp;\\&amp;&amp; Aj=0A_j = 0Aj​=0, where &amp;\\&amp;&amp; denotes the bitwise AND operator.\nChef wants to know the **lexicographically minimum** array that can be obtained using any (possibly zero) number of given swaps.\n\nNote: An array XXX of size NNN is lexicographically smaller than an array YYY of size NNN if Xi&lt;YiX_i \\lt Y_iXi​&lt;Yi​, where iii is the smallest index on which XXX and YYY differ.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input consists of an integer NNN - denoting the size of array AAA.\nThe second line of input consists of NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_{N}A1​,A2​,…,AN​ - denoting array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput the lexicographically minimum array that can be obtained using any (possibly zero) number of given swaps.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤1061 \\leq N \\leq 10^{6}1≤N≤106",
      "1≤Ai&lt;2201 \\leq A_{i} \\lt 2^{20}1≤Ai​&lt;220"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1 5 2",
        "output": "1 2 5",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe lexicographically minimum array that can be obtained is [1,2,5][1, 2, 5][1,2,5].\nIt can be obtained by swapping A2A_2A2​ and A3A_3A3​ since A2A_2A2​ &\\&& A3=0A_3 = 0A3​=0."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 6 2",
        "output": "2 6 2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe lexicographically minimum array that can be obtained is [2,6,2][2, 6, 2][2,6,2]. No swaps can be made in the given array."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4 \n8 7 16 9",
        "output": "7 8 9 16",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe lexicographically minimum array that can be obtained is [7,8,9,16][7, 8, 9, 16][7,8,9,16].\nThe swaps required to obtain [7,8,9,16][7, 8, 9, 16][7,8,9,16] are:\n\nA1A_1A1​ and A2A_2A2​ since A1A_1A1​ &\\&& A2=0A_2 = 0A2​=0. The array becomes [7,8,16,9][7, 8, 16, 9][7,8,16,9].\nA3A_3A3​ and A4A_4A4​ since A3A_3A3​ &\\&& A4=0A_4 = 0A4​=0. The array becomes [7,8,9,16][7, 8, 9, 16][7,8,9,16]."
      }
    ]
  },
